# The source pages under android/data/sources are content-addressed: tools/extract_data.js and
# tools/extract_qiershi.js record their SHA256 in android/data/extracted/provenance.json, and CI
# fails when a regeneration no longer matches what is committed. Any line-ending conversion would
# change those bytes, so the pages are explicitly excluded from text normalisation.
android/data/sources/*.html -text

# The two files above are copies of the pages published at the repository root (v2.20/), and
# data/extracted/*.json is generated from them at build time. None of it is hand-written source, so
# keep it out of the repository language statistics -- otherwise these ~1.8 MB of data dominate the
# bar and make the Kotlin app look like a rounding error.
android/data/sources/*.html linguist-vendored
android/data/extracted/*.json linguist-generated
